# Expectation record for 11_literals_and_strings/003_wide_and_unicode_literals.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 003_wide_and_unicode_literals
area               = 11_literals_and_strings
description        = Wide, UTF-8, 16-bit and 32-bit literals indexed in place
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
No header is included, so none of the three C11 character type names is written: every
literal is indexed in place and every element is cast explicitly to long long or unsigned
long long, so no conversion narrows and no printed value depends on a target's wide
character width.  No literal is modified and every index is inside its literal's size.  The
source file is pure US-ASCII, and all non-ASCII characters appear only as
universal-character-name escapes.  No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
